OCMAT 1
# Written by the Aver Engine editor.
# NeonDistrict: "Low Poly Skyscrapers" by exleute (@exleute), CC BY 4.0 -- https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/low-poly-skyscrapers-4d51f4281a8649528569021411820d28
NAME NeonDistrict_sf71_windows
SHADER standard
BLEND opaque
CULL none
FLAGS twosided=1 castshadow=1 worlduv=0

PARAM baseColorFactor 0.779766 0.8917 0.903545 1
# Not metal: its metal/rough map marks the panes metal 1 / rough 0, a black mirror.
PARAM metallicFactor 0
PARAM roughnessFactor 0
# Emissive in engine units: 1 = a white wall in full sun, about 33,000 cd/m2. Peak 0.03 = about 1,000 cd/m2:
# every window pane of the seven towers (4,088 individual quads; the black frames are separate geometry, so only the panes glow): lit office floors at night. No emissive factor or map in the glTF, so the installer makes them flat white. One material is shared by all seven towers, so they cannot get different strengths without duplicating the material per tower. tower_03 has ribbon windows, which read as continuous glowing bands.
PARAM emissiveFactor 0.03 0.03 0.03
PARAM normalScale 1
PARAM occlusionStrength 1
PARAM reflectance 0.04
PARAM f90 1
PARAM ior 1.5
PARAM transmission 0
PARAM uvTiling 200
